-- title:
--   Degree of the Γ₁(M)∩Γ₀(p) function field over Γ₀(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero. For a congruence subgroup $\Gamma \le \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ and a field $K$, [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) denotes the intermediate field of $K((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $K$ all quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_g$, where $f,g$ are modular forms of some weight $k$ for the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}(2,\mathbb{R})$, $p_f,p_g$ are integral power series that are $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$ in the sense of `IsIntegralQExp`, and the series attached to $p_g$ is nonzero; [`ModularCurve.x1x0FunctionFieldC K M t`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L142) is this field for $\Gamma = \Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(t)$. Further, [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) is the intermediate field of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the image of $F₀ \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ under the coefficientwise map induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$. Let $K_1, K_2$ be intermediate fields of $L((q))$ over $L$ with $K_1$ equal to the base change to $L$ of the field for $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and $K_2$ equal to the base change to $L$ of the field for $\Gamma_0(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Then the relative degree `IntermediateField.relfinrank K₂ K₁`, that is the degree of $K_1$ over $K_2 \sqcap K_1$, equals the index of the subgroup generated by $-1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$.
--
--   This is the function-field form of the statement that the modular curve for $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$ covers $X_0(Mp)$ with degree equal to the index of $\pm 1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ (numerically $\varphi(M)/2$ for $M \ge 3$), the covering group being the diamond operators modulo $\pm 1$. It is used in the comparison of residue-field degrees at the Gauss valuation of this extension and in the computation of the order of a group acting faithfully on it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_relfinrank_laurentBaseChange_gamma0_mul_x1x0FunctionFieldC_eq_index.lean

